section.subsection:
The commission shall adjust a taxing entity's certified tax rate as provided in Subsection (3) if the county legislative body in which the taxing entity is located certifies to the commission in writing that:

the taxing entity's assessment roll contained a clerical error;
the county adjusted the clerical error on the assessment roll;
the taxing entity's actual collections for the year were different than the taxing entity's budgeted collections for the year; and
the taxing entity notified the county legislative body of the clerical error after the county treasurer provided the tax notices under Section 59-2-1317, but no later than 60 days after the day on which the county treasurer made the final annual settlement with the taxing entity under Section 59-2-1365.
